  "title": "The Reforming King of Judah",
  "era": "divided-kingdom",
  "lifespan": "c. 649–609 BC",
  "summary": "Josiah was one of the most godly kings in the kingdom of Judah. He became king at eight years old and carried out a comprehensive religious reform after the Book of the Law was found in the temple. He removed idolatry from the land, renewed the covenant with the Lord, but fell in battle against Pharaoh Neco at Megiddo.",
